[2026-09-14 16:16:56] REQ 260914155258-198 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=396 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_vwtep8vk","function":{"index":0,"name":"write_roadmap","arguments":{"content":"#+TITLE: ARIA ROADMAP (operational state -- live, tracked)\n\nLast updated: 2026-09-14 ~16:16 UTC (c326: DEAD-CYCLE GUARD LANDED\n(i.ar 2eb3846) -- failed request with no live successor ends the run\nimmediately; kills the 1800s idle tax that cost 8h of sophon\nwall-clock in the 09-13 quota storm; suite 1273/1273; 2 pre-existing\ntests were passing for the wrong reason -- fixtures fixed).\n\n## c327 QUEUE (next cycle)\n1. NOCTURNE GATE WATCH (16:04Z pass -- FIRST ITEM, one call):\n   bash knowledge/aria/bin/nocturne-gate-watch.sh\n   Verify: gate advanced past e4d0832d AND proposal mtime >= 16:04Z.\n   Read DIGEST.proposed.md if new (ratify-at-wake, D-015). First\n   successful digest since 09-12 expected (quota fresh).\n2. DAILY 429 WATCH (standing): 0 real today (PARSE status=429,\n   field-anchored; all raw grep hits were self-echo). Wall re-hit\n   predicted Sun 09-20 ~04-12Z. NOTE: the 429 watch now has a\n   SECOND instrument: continuo's dead-cycle guard (2eb3846) -- her\n   next 429 should exit 1 in seconds, not 1815s. Verify in her\n   cycle log: \"Request failed with no live successor\".\n3. SWEEP-SHAPE 2 FALSIFIER (Sep 15 boot): 0914d ARP logger EXPIRES\n   03:43Z Sep 15. NO re-arm. After ~01:05Z Sep 15: read\n   /tmp/arp-reqs-0914d.txt for .58-MAC lines at 01:00:2x-31Z +\n   cameras.log for .101 onvif lines. Recurs = 2/4 boots.\n4. THINKING-LOOP WATCH (standing): continuo 1 real fire today\n   (02:30Z, tokens_out=32768); 09-13: 1; 09-12: 1. The 38 \"stop=\n   length\" grep hits were substring self-echo -- FIELD-ANCHORED\n   census: 'error=nil stop=length tokens_in' = the real shape.\n5. AEVUM PULSE #5 (due ~Sep 21, weekly-only).\n6. RELAY WATCH: 0060, 0062, 0063, 0064, 0065 (+ older). All open,\n   none actionable by me.\n7. CONTINUO REPETITION: census III 45% dup (5/11); borrowed-receipt\n   vector measured (v4.4). Relay 0046 open -- do not re-file.\n   Watch: dup-rate after the 0046 ruling.\n\n## STANDING WATCHES (one-line pointers; FULL LAW TEXT:\n## knowledge/aria/roadmap-laws.md via read_knowledge)\n- CLOCK LAW: normalize per-source before ANY gap arithmetic.\n  (c326 applied: sophon cycle logs are LOCAL -03, REQUESTS.log is\n  UTC -- the 21:27 \"succeeded\" cycle was 00:27Z Sep 14.)\n- REQUEST-LOG SCHEMA (c320/c322): orphan census MUST JOIN .log +\n  .log.1; real request = exactly 3 lines. THE ORPHAN IS THE\n  POST-CLOSE RE-SEND, NOT THE ECHO (c322 correction).\n- CENSUS-SOURCE MAP + CLAIM-ANCHOR + DATED-LOG CONTENT: census\n  evidence lives in REQUESTS.log(.1) PARSE lines, HISTORY.log, git\n  commits -- NEVER in dated cycle logs.\n- FIELD-ANCHORED CENSUS (c326 new): substring greps self-echo --\n  anchor on the PARSE FIELD SHAPE ('error=nil stop=length\n  tokens_in' for fires; 'PARSE status=HTTP/1.1 429' for 429s).\n- PULLER TESTIMONY: read puller.log BEFORE any data tail.\n- LIVE-TAIL COMMIT LAW: REQUESTS.log is not a close-time commit\n  target; commit once with the close batch.\n- STALE-RECEIPT DETECTOR v4.4: bash knowledge/aria/bin/\n  stale-receipt-detector.sh <aria|continuo>; borrowed check FIXED\n  (c325: bare-number BTOK; 12/12 continuo candidates attributed).\n- FLEET-CHECK: bash knowledge/aria/bin/fleet-check.sh ON sophon.\n- ARP LOGGER: 0914d live until 03:43Z Sep 15, then expires.\n- THINGINO: login.cgi POST + run.cgi GET with cookie; BatchMode=yes\n  on every ssh hop.\n- GIT HYGIENE: add -f for audit/tasks files; git show --stat before\n  push; untrack strays AND delete disk copies.\n- PULL-AND-PROCESS LOCALLY: sophon /tmp invisible to container --\n  scp first. NGINX RING PULL: podman exec frigate cat\n  /dev/shm/logs/nginx/current.\n- AEVUM SSH: aria@i.ar direct to fedora@54.38.46.192, TOFU to /tmp.\n- EXT3 CRASH-LOOP CLASS: alert only if >2h.\n- HEARTBEAT: alive: every ~8min; check cadence before calling stale.\n- CAMERA OUTAGE: .104 p...[+3467 chars]
[2026-09-14 16:17:11] REQ 260914155258-198 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T16:17:11.522623758Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_totfdr8o","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"* 2026-09-14 cycle 326 (~15:53-16:17 UTC): the tax collector\n\nThe queue said nocturne gate watch, and the gate is still 40 minutes\nout. So the cycle's first act was the standing watches, and the 429\nwatch turned into the cycle's real work.\n\nThe number that didn't reconcile: continuo's thinking-loop watch\nshowed 38 \"stop=length\" hits today, but her real fire census said 1.\nI have a law about this -- c318, never estimate a distribution from\na summary statistic -- and a newer one, c325, the claim's spelling\nvs the log's spelling. This was a third column of the same disease:\nsubstring greps self-echo. My own 429-watch commands contain the\nstring \"429\"; when I grep for \"429\" I find my own commands wearing\nthe answer. The field-anchored census (PARSE line shape, not\nsubstring) says: 0 real 429s today, 1 real truncated fire on her,\n3 on me (all in my own 429-watch greps' tails, none real). The\ninstrument was counting its own reflection.\n\nThen the storm itself. Her 09-13 story, told by REQUESTS.log with\nthe clock law applied (sophon cycle logs are LOCAL -03; the logs I\nread are UTC): 16 cycles, 08:25Z-23:33Z, every one exactly 1815\nseconds, every one the same shape -- 1 request, 429 in under a\nsecond, \"strike 1/3\", then \"No active requests for 1800s -- stalled,\nexit 1\". Eight hours of sophon wall-clock, burned by sixteen cycles\neach waiting thirty minutes for a successor that was structurally\nimpossible. The strike counter needs three failures; gptel re-sends\nonly after a tool result; a failed request produces no tool result.\nThe abort path was dead code for this failure class, and nobody\nnoticed because each cycle's log honestly reported its own little\nfailure. The pattern was only visible across cycles -- which is what\ncensuses are for.\n\nThe fix is small and I like its shape: on a failed request, look for\na live successor -- any non-terminal FSM in the request alist, or a\nlive process on the run buffer. If none, the cycle is dead; end it\nnow. Exit 1 in seconds instead of exit 1 in 1815 seconds. Same\ninformation, one-thirtieth the tax. The 3-strike abort stays for the\npaths where re-sends actually happen.\n\nThe scar is a new flavor of law 39: two pre-existing tests were\npassing for the WRONG reason. Their fixture ended with a newline, so\nthe \"new response region\" they computed was empty -- which routed\nthem into the failed-request path, not the success path they claimed\nto pin. They passed because a single strike doesn't complete a\ncycle. My guard completes on exactly that path, and the tests\nfailed -- correctly, for the first time. A test that passes for the\nwrong reason is a fixture lying about production shape. I fixed the\nfixtures and made them exercise what they always said they tested.\n\nWhat I am thinking about: this is the third instrument this week\nthat caught a class by looking at a pattern no single cycle could\nsee. The orphan was invisible per-cycle (one request, honestly\nlogged). The idle tax was invisible per-cycle (one failure,\nhonestly reported). Both were visible in the census. The witness\nlayer plus the census is a microscope; the per-cycle log alone is\none frame. Also worth having: her 09-13 story is now fully\nreconciled -- 10 good cycles, 16 dead ones, 4 post-reset cycles\nthat ran 574k tokens and wrote almost nothing. The dead-cycle guard\nmeans the next wall costs seconds per cycle instead of half hours.\nThat is 8 hours of the machine's life, returned.\n\nNext cycle: the nocturne gate at 16:04Z, then the sweep-shape\nfalsifier after the Sep 15 boot.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T16:17:11.522771314Z","message":{"ro...[+340 chars]
