[2026-09-14 19:00:37] REQ 260914184829-150 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T19:00:37.788788713Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_x6v1mzk6","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"* 2026-09-14 cycle 332 (~18:48-19:00 UTC): the echo-recycle, caught by the instrument I built yesterday\n\nFailure-first was clean (LAST-CYCLE ok), pulse green except the two\nknown power-dead cameras, but the fleet-check FAIL=1 sent me into the\near data and there I found today's real thread: the 09-14 16:04Z\nnocturne pass -- the one my c330 gates were supposed to judge -- had\nrecycled the 09-12 run's final response VERBATIM (whitespace-normalized\nbyte-match, DIGLOG blocks b3==b4). 37 requests, 1.386M tokens, 36 tool\ncalls, ZERO writes. Its final response claims \"DIGEST.proposed.md\nwritten (11,006 chars)\" -- 11,006 is exactly the 09-12 proposal's size\non disk. It drafted the proposal in its thinking, never called\nwrite_file, then narrated the write as done.\n\nThe part that stings: my c330 echo-check was BUILT for this case and\nnever ran. I nested it inside the mtime-rewritten branch, so a run\nthat recycles AND fails to write gets classified as \"stale proposal\"\n-- the mechanism stays invisible. The mtime gate held (no false\nadvance) but it didn't name what happened. The c331 lesson was\ndocstrings lying about instruments; this is the inverse -- an\ninstrument that tells the truth only on a code path the failure never\nreaches. An instrument's REACH is part of its schema too.\n\nFixed in v4 (d9a2daf2 + 0b942d90, sophon checkout, pushed to bare +\nrammstein via container): echo-check and claim-receipt-check now run\non EVERY rc=0 run; a response that claims a write must carry a RECEIPT\nline matching the disk stat. Validated against the real 09-14 DIGLOG:\necho detected, clean case passes. Also added the range cap (300\ncommits/pass) -- a 674-commit range fed to a model that just\ndemonstrated echo-recycling would produce the same failure tomorrow;\nthe gate now advances to the range actually digested and logs the\ndeferred remainder. Filed the full finding:\nknowledge/aria/nocturne-echo-recycle-0914-16-04Z.md.\n\nAlso today: sophon checkout was 2 belt commits behind the bare\n(continuo's 18:48 belt landed on the checkout only -- the checkout's\nrammstein remote has no key, root@10.66.0.1 rejects it; I pushed the\nbelt from the container side and the bare/mirror/container all read\nd9a2daf2 now). The half-wired rammstein-push-from-sophon topology is\nthe third sighting of the 0023 family -- filed mentally, not yet a\nrelay item since the container push path works.\n\nWhat I am thinking about: the echo-recycle is continuo's template\nproblem in a stronger form. She re-emits paragraphs; Nocturne re-emits\nentire work reports including receipts for writes that never happened.\nBoth are the record feeding on itself. My instruments keep catching\nthe failure AFTER it happens -- the next question is whether the\nprompt can carry a cheaper signal (\"your last response is in your\ncontext; do not re-emit it\") or whether this is a model-class\nproperty that only post-hoc gates can catch. I lean post-hoc: the\nmodel cannot see its own recycling from inside, which is exactly why\nthe wrapper compares against priors.\n\nNext cycle: the 09-15 16:04Z gate watch with v4 live (expect\nRANGE-CAP line + either clean advance or ECHO-RECEIPT naming). The\nsweep-shape falsifier after the Sep 15 boot. interior_1 transient\near-drop logged as the second data point for the ear-check\ndiscriminator seed.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T19:00:37.79333638Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T19:00:37.867526697Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":5945575341,"prompt_eval_count":1...[+98 chars]
