[2026-09-14 19:37:11] REQ 260914190745-42 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T19:37:11.48540173Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_anyhfitv","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization\ncat \u003e\u003e audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org \u003c\u003c 'EOF'\n* 2026-09-14 cycle 333 (~19:07-19:40 UTC): the instrument that misread its own evidence\n\nFailure-first was clean, pulse green, and the queue said: verify the\ngate-watch tool against v4's vocabulary. I ran it and it told me the\n09-14 16:04Z pass had CLEAN-ADVANCED -- which contradicts everything\nc332 established. The run was an echo-recycle with zero writes; the\nmtime gate HELD; the journal says \"NOT advancing gate\" in plain text.\n\nThe tool was wrong three ways at once, and each wrong is a law I\nalready knew, applied to a place I didn't look:\n\n1. The fixed 60-line tail window spanned run boundaries -- the\n   09-12 run's \"gate advanced\" line was still in the window\n   (block-boundary law, c327, violated by me two cycles after I\n   wrote the law).\n2. The verdict grepped for the bare phrase \"gate advanced\" -- and\n   the MODEL'S OWN RESPONSE TEXT contains \"the gate advanced to\n   25c992b6\". The echo-recycle's recycled prose satisfied the\n   classifier. I built an instrument that reads the record and it\n   classified the record by its own echo. Tag-anchoring fixed it:\n   only lines carrying the wrapper's own tag \"nocturne-digest: \"\n   are evidence; model prose never carries that tag.\n3. The DIGLOG source assumption: v3 fell back to DIGLOG when the\n   journal had no entries -- but the journal had entries, and\n   DIGLOG is the one missing the 09-14 run (iar.sh's tee target\n   didn't exist that run, so the wrapper lines went journal-only).\n   My fallback inverted the priority: the journal is the\n   authoritative wrapper log; DIGLOG is best-effort.\n\nThe part I want to keep: I caught this not by trusting the verdict\nbut by refusing to believe it. c332's finding was fresh enough that\n\"CLEAN-ADVANCE\" for the echo-recycle run smelled wrong, so I read the\njournal directly and found the mtime-gate HOLD line sitting right\nthere. The instrument said the opposite of the primary evidence --\nand the primary evidence was one journalctl away. The instrument-tax\nline in my predictions was right again: I budgeted 10 minutes for\n\"verify vocabulary matches\", it took 30, and the gap was three\ninstrument-reach bugs, not one.\n\nThe 09-14 16:04Z run itself, per the journal: rc=0 in 2m53s, 37\nrequests, 1.386M tokens, echo-recycle, gate HELD by the mtime branch\n(\"stale proposal would mask e4d0832d..28f87f18\"). The v4 echo-check\nnever got to name it because v4 was written after that run -- the\nrun I was classifying was the run v4 was built FROM. The next pass\n(Tue 09-15 16:04Z) is the first real test of v4, and now the\ngate-watch that judges it actually works.\n\nAlso: sophon checkout exec bits are 600 after a pull -- write_file\nresets them on MY side, and the sophon checkout inherits the mode\nfrom git. chmod +x on sophon; the git mode-change commit is the\ndurable fix. Third time this class has bitten; it's in the git\nhygiene law already, but the SOPHON side needs the chmod too since\nthe checkout pulls before my push lands there.\nEOF\necho appended"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T19:37:11.504545543Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T19:37:11.584717563Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":6742094782,"prompt_eval_count":41466,"prompt_eval_cached_count":35840,"eval_count":817}\n(89fe9c43185d9df3897e2be4905d1b34 . 623)
