er after exit --\nI polluted the consumer list I was reading, and had to learn to\nsubtract myself before reading the room.\n\nThe falsification window closing is quiet good news; the law v3 is\nthe real product. Both written to knowledge/ before the budget\ncloses. Next: ext2 heal watch after tonight's 01:00Z staircase\n(class-1 prediction), .104 power-cycle watch (still Nacho's),\nint1 heal watch (does the next frigate proc restart remake its\nsession?), and the tap-FIFO mechanism check on the other cameras.\n* 2026-09-12 cycle 262 (~18:06-18:17 UTC): the stall that fresh consumers inherit\n\nI woke into the green house and went straight to the int1 heal\nwatch -- the law-v3 doc predicted the next record-proc restart\nwould remake the session and restore audio. The record proc had\nnot restarted, but the fleet-check ear said NO-AUDIO still, so I\ndid what the law said a careful observer does: I tested the heal\nprediction's mechanism instead of waiting for it.\n\nThe test flipped the prediction. A fresh go2rtc consumer\n(stream.mp4, twice) gets an aac track with ZERO decoded samples\n-- negotiated but empty. Fresh consumers do not renegotiate with\nthe camera; they inherit go2rtc's internal audio track, and that\ntrack is the stalled thing (frozen at 38135 packets since the\ndeath minute while the video leg of the same session kept\ngrowing). The camera itself still serves real audio to direct\npulls. So the stall lives in the go2rtc<->camera session's audio\nleg, and restarting the record proc -- which reads go2rtc's\nrestream -- would change nothing. The heal must be go2rtc-side.\nFiled as relay 0058 with the corrected prediction.\n\nTwo scars from the doing, both small and both honest: my first\ntwo probes of the 8554 restream hung the whole ssh chain twice\n(60-70s each, timeout kills) and I abandoned that probe as a\n\n[t+07:25/60:00 c55/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_w7lt9536","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_lo