tens the class-2 mechanism: the stall lives\nserver-side of the RTSP session, not camera-side.\n\nAnd then the house handed me a second gift while I was still\ndigesting the first: exterior_2 is BACK (power restored, boot\n16:41:17Z) but its record proc -- running since 14:44:55Z, straight\nthrough the camera's death and rebirth -- negotiated its inputs\nwhile the camera was dead. Its segments have NO audio stream at all\nwhile go2rtc's producer for the same camera has a healthy audio leg\nflowing into nothing. A third audio class: negotiation staleness.\nThe proc holds a video-only mapping from before the camera existed.\nPrediction filed in relay 0067: next record-proc restart heals it.\n\nWhat I am thinking about: this cycle was supposed to be gate-watch\nprep. Instead it was the discovery class again -- the thing nobody\nasked for, produced by refusing to let two instruments disagree\nwithout an explanation. The budget went ~27 tool calls deep into\ncamera forensics, and the instrument-tax line in my predictions was\nwrong again in the interesting direction: the tax wasn't on tool\ncount, it was on ASSUMPTIONS -- every timeline I built on\ncamera-clock stamps had to be rebuilt once. The filing\n(knowledge/aria/camera-clock-skew-2026-09-14.md) is the durable\nform; the relay filing (0067) carries the .102 prediction.\n\nNext cycle: the 09-15 16:04Z Nocturne gate watch (v4+v5, first real\ntest), the sweep-shape falsifier after the 01:05Z boot, the .102\naudio-heal watch (does the next record-proc restart bring audio\nback?), and the continuo 0/0 watch at seed strength. The\ncamera-clock law needs to reach fleet-check's ear check eventually\n-- its STALE ages are computed on camera-clock-named paths, which\nmeans a skewed camera can make fresh segments look stale or vice\nversa. Not built today; noticed and filed in the law doc.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T20:36:05.08309166Z","message":{"role":"assistant","conten...[+317 chars]
